WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:10.600
AWS Public Change Alerting matches public AWS announcements to
configured services and risk phrases, then sends the results to
Slack.

2
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:19.570
M1 proved delivery, M2 added retention and replay controls, and
M3 established readiness for the reviewed deployment.

3
00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:23.117
EventBridge schedules three Lambdas.

4
00:00:23.237 --> 00:00:31.812
The watcher fetches approved feeds, matches service aliases and
risk phrases, and records candidates before advancing
checkpoints.

5
00:00:31.932 --> 00:00:36.182
The dispatcher sends due delivery records to SQS FIFO.

6
00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:41.402
The queue invokes the Slack worker, which sends the message and
records the outcome.

7
00:00:41.522 --> 00:00:47.572
The reconciler recovers overdue work and marks expired sends as
delivery unknown.

8
00:00:47.692 --> 00:00:53.667
A fifth Lambda, shadow, evaluates the same feed policy in memory
for deployment checks.

9
00:00:54.667 --> 00:01:00.242
DynamoDB keeps checkpoints and delivery history after queue
messages are consumed.

10
00:01:00.362 --> 00:01:06.137
Conditional writes coordinate leases, deduplication, and retries
across Lambdas.

11
00:01:06.257 --> 00:01:10.107
SQS provides transport and destination ordering.

12
00:01:10.227 --> 00:01:16.252
S3 holds exact configuration releases and retained feed
responses for replay.

13
00:01:16.372 --> 00:01:22.822
CloudWatch collects runtime logs and metrics; alarms notify the
operator through SNS.

14
00:01:22.942 --> 00:01:29.392
CloudTrail has a narrower role here: proving which table and
timestamp a recovery request used.

15
00:01:29.512 --> 00:01:31.987
It doesn't prove restored contents.

16
00:01:32.107 --> 00:01:38.907
Terraform defines the resources and scoped IAM roles, including
access to Slack credentials.

17
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:48.475
M1's live cohort produced twelve Slack posts, each with one
network attempt, and twelve posted records in DynamoDB.

18
00:01:48.595 --> 00:01:57.595
A separate recovery exercise completed a pending delivery and
moved an expired send lease to delivery unknown without another
Slack call.

19
00:01:57.715 --> 00:02:01.590
The fixed load run created fifty records in ten minutes.

20
00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:04.660
The owner also received the alarm email.

21
00:02:05.633 --> 00:02:09.458
M2 addressed what happens as history accumulates.

22
00:02:09.578 --> 00:02:17.103
The migration added expiry dates to one-hundred-and-sixty-four
old rows, leaving the four active checkpoints alone.

23
00:02:17.223 --> 00:02:23.973
Retained-source replay now binds one saved response and
inspected state into a reviewed plan.

24
00:02:24.093 --> 00:02:27.968
It can fill missing records but can't touch feed checkpoints.

25
00:02:28.088 --> 00:02:30.688
No live source replay was applied.

26
00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:40.917
The matcher scored twenty-nine true-positive service and risk
pairs, with no false positives or false negatives, on
forty-seven labeled items.

27
00:02:41.037 --> 00:02:43.562
That passes the global thresholds.

28
00:02:43.682 --> 00:02:52.882
But six configured pairs have no historical positive, so that
score doesn't establish recall on real AWS wording for those
pairs.

29
00:02:53.867 --> 00:02:58.767
M3 reused earlier evidence where the changes still supported it.

30
00:02:58.887 --> 00:03:01.887
The missing test was application rollback.

31
00:03:02.007 --> 00:03:09.582
With durable execution paused, we switched all five Lambdas to
the qualified predecessor and back to the successor.

32
00:03:09.702 --> 00:03:16.802
One shadow run per version returned the same eight candidate
identities from two-hundred-and-forty items.

33
00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:22.275
The stopped-state digests matched, then we restored normal
operation.

34
00:03:22.395 --> 00:03:29.220
The fixed observation window passed, all twenty-eight alarms
were healthy, and Terraform showed no changes.

35
00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:36.915
The owner accepted readiness for one environment and Slack
destination at three-hundred delivery requests per hour.

36
00:03:37.035 --> 00:03:40.710
Live service on restored tables remains unproved.
